# EXCEPTION 3, same shape and the same evidence standard as EXCEPTION 2 above, applied to
# `platform/` (lines 77-81) instead of `command-center/` (line 76).
#
# `platform/` sat OUTSIDE the published-command gate's corpus, which is exactly how this got
# past everything: a committed report could publish `python platform/.../_probe_x.py` and no
# gate would notice the target was ignored. SLOP build round 3 widened the corpus to
# `platform/` and the gate immediately named 10 unrunnable citations. Seven of them are the
# files below -- they exist on ONE disk, and a clone cannot run a single one.
#
# Only the CITED scripts are negated; every other `platform/**/_probe_*.py` stays ignored,
# because absence of a citation is not evidence of worthlessness. The eighth surfaced target,
# `platform/lib/ssot/verify.py`, is NOT here: it does not exist on disk at all, so it is a
# baseline row with an owner rather than a file to commit.
#
# Committed BYTE-UNCHANGED, exactly as EXCEPTION 2 argues. Measured at the CI pin
# ruff@0.15.17: all seven pass `ruff check` clean, and six fail `ruff format --check`. Those
# six are listed under `[format]` in ruff.toml -- a FORMAT-ONLY exclusion, which is narrower
# than EXCEPTION 2's `extend-exclude` because `ruff check` stays live on them.
!platform/architecture/_probe_crossvendor_alias_hole.py
!platform/architecture/_probe_dr_acyclic.py
!platform/architecture/_probe_dr_bucketedge.py
!platform/architecture/_probe_dr_catalog.py
!platform/architecture/_probe_dr_scheduling.py
!platform/council/presets/_probe_preset_validation.py
!platform/lib/workflows/_gen_bp5.py

# plugin build output. The distributable ZIP is regenerated by one command
# (`python platform/plugin/astplugin.py build`) and is byte-identical for identical content,
# so the artifact itself is not source. Its measured size/sha/member list is recorded in the
# tracked platform/plugin/PACKAGE-MEASUREMENT.json.
platform/plugin/dist/

# harness/ast-integrate -- the P2 (G-1) repair tree captured 2026-09-02 by the `ast-integrate`
# mapping in scripts/sync-from-live.ps1, so the 2007-unit measurement can run in a cloud Linux
# worker from the repo. The append-only repair log and the wave logs under it ARE the P2 audit
# trail, so the global `*.log` rule (line 3) must not silently drop them at `git add` time.
# Mirrors the mapping's KeepFilePatterns = @('*.log'). Everything else the mapping excludes is
# listed in harness/ast-integrate/CAPTURE-EXCLUSIONS.md.
!harness/ast-integrate/**/*.log
